int d = k % n;

You should not use k % n.

For this problem, if k > n, the entire array is reversed as one group (depending on the exact problem specification). 
More importantly, if k == n, your code gets:

d = k % n = 0;

Then:

i += d;

becomes:

i += 0;

and your loop becomes infinite. so dont use that .....


